course: dictionary
lesson: 13163
title: Forthcoming: soon, ready, or willing to talk
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Forthcoming» is an adjective, a describing word, and it is a little formal. It has three meanings, so the context tells you which one fits.
explain: Meaning one is coming soon. In «the forthcoming holiday», the holiday is about to happen. Ask yourself: is it coming up soon? If yes, that is the meaning.
explain: Meaning two is ready or given when needed. «No help was forthcoming» means that no help came when people needed it.
explain: Meaning three is willing to talk and give information. «He was not forthcoming about where he had been» means he did not want to say where he went.
fact: Forthcoming is an adjective, so it describes a noun such as an event, a trip or a person.
fact: «Forthcoming» means happening or coming soon, as in «the forthcoming trip».
fact: «Forthcoming» can also mean ready or given when needed, as in «help was forthcoming».
fact: «Forthcoming» can mean willing to talk and share information, so «not forthcoming» means someone kept quiet.
fact: It is a slightly formal word, so you will often see it in letters, reports and stories.
exercise: «The forthcoming trip to the museum is next week.» What does forthcoming mean here? | Ready to use | Willing to talk | Lost and never found | *Happening soon
exercise: «When Mia asked for a pen, one was forthcoming at once.» What does forthcoming mean here? | Very loud | Lost and gone | *Ready and given when needed | Happening next year
exercise: «Ben was not forthcoming about the broken vase.» What does forthcoming suggest? | Very tall | Hungry | Ready to help | *Unwilling to say what happened
test: «The forthcoming concert starts at seven.» Which meaning fits forthcoming here? | *Coming soon | Finished last year | Very quiet | Hidden under the stage
test: «The police asked questions, but the boy was not forthcoming.» What does not forthcoming mean? | He was very loud | He was hungry | *He did not want to say much | He gave lots of facts and details
exam: «The forthcoming book comes out in May.» Which meaning of forthcoming fits this sentence best? | Very old | Ready when needed | *Happening soon | Willing to talk
